course: dictionary
lesson: 14428
title: Overturned: upside down or changed
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Overturned is a word you will see in news, stories and sports reports. Its clues are in the word itself: over and turned. When something is overturned, it has been turned over, so it is now upside down or lying on its side. «The strong wind blew the bin and it overturned on the path.» The bin is no longer standing up.
explain: Overturned also works in another way. When someone with more power changes a decision, that decision is overturned. «The judge overturned the first ruling after reading the new evidence.» The first ruling was not kept. It was cancelled and replaced.
explain: Look at the words around it. If you see a boat, a car or a chair, overturned probably means upside down or on its side. If you see a judge, a court or a video replay, it probably means a decision has been changed. Then swap in your meaning to check it still makes sense.
fact: Overturned means turned upside down or onto its side.
fact: «An overturned boat» is a boat lying upside down in the water.
fact: An overturned decision has been changed or cancelled by someone with more authority, such as a judge.
fact: Overturn is the verb, and overturned is its past form. It can also work as an adjective, as in «overturned chairs».
fact: In a messy scene, «overturned chairs» means chairs knocked over and lying on their sides or backs.
exercise: «The lorry overturned on the motorway.» What does overturned mean here? | Filled with food | Driven very fast | *Turned upside down or onto its side | Parked neatly in a row
exercise: «The judge overturned the decision.» What happened to the decision? | It was forgotten | *It was changed or cancelled | It was made again, exactly the same | It was read out loud to the crowd
exercise: «The overturned chairs lay across the floor after the party.» Copy the word that tells you the chairs were knocked over. | lay | *overturned | floor | across
test: Which word is closest in meaning to overturned, as in «an overturned bin»? | Sold | *Upended | Mended | Polished
test: «The goal was overturned after the video replay.» What does this tell you? | The goal was painted gold | The goal was kicked very hard | The goal was scored twice | *The goal was cancelled after a check
exam: Which sentence uses overturned to mean a decision was changed? | The chairs were overturned after the game | *The appeal court overturned the sentence | The bus overturned in the car park | The cat overturned the milk jug
